{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning","id":928581,"title":"Why care about Making spells when you have Patterning?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-08T21:12:09-07:00","id":928581,"title":"Why care about Making spells when you have Patterning?","content":"I'm trying to understand why you'd ever cast a Making spell, when a Patterning spell is easier and can accomplish the same thing. For example, why create a spirit ex nihilo, when you could use a Patterning spell to transform a mote of essence into the same spirit? Why create a Hallow with a Making spell when you should be able to transform a point of mana into a hallow with a Patterning spell? Why create an anchor connecting you to a ghost when you can transform a drop of ectoplasm into that very same anchor?<br /> <br /> The book seems to operate on the assumption that Making spells can somehow do more than Patterning spells, but I don't see anything in the descriptions of the practices that would suggest this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T21:54:09-07:00","id":928590,"title":"","content":"Making spells in many instances can create things that are Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:31:01-07:00","id":928597,"title":"","content":"If you don't have the raw materials you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T23:40:45-07:00","id":928615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928597#post928597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't have the raw materials you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any limit to Patterning spells, except that the target and result both fall under the arcanum. When could you possibly be lacking in raw materials?<br /> <br /> Prime: Yantras are everywhere<br /> Matter: Use a rock<br /> Life: Use a blade of grass, a drop of blood, or the microorganisms in your spit.<br /> Forces: Use some light<br /> Spirit: Grab a mote of essence from the Shadow<br /> Death: Grab a drop of ectoplasm from Twilight<br /> Fate: Grab a fork from the kitchen and use its destiny.<br /> Time: Time is everywhere<br /> Space: Sympathetic connections are everywhere<br /> Mind: Use a thought, or an ant's mind.<br /> <br /> Voila. If you need a hallow, just pull out a quarter and transform the quarter's Yantra symbolism into a Hallow. If you need an extradimensional space, pull out the quarter again and transform one of its sympathetic connections into the extradimensional space. If you need a destiny, transform the quarter's destiny into a completely different destiny for someone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928590#post928590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making spells in many instances can create things that are Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's incidental, not an inherent property of Making spells. There's plenty of counter-examples, like Platonic Form or Soul Jar. Which spells are lasting and which are not is mainly determined by whether the spell needs to be Lasting to be useful. Creating non-lasting tass, for example, is not a terribly practical way to store mana, which is why it's now Lasting in 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 07-09-2016, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T00:28:50-07:00","id":928625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928590#post928590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making spells in many instances can create things that are Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T00:32:31-07:00","id":928627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928625#post928625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T01:38:54-07:00","id":928641,"title":"","content":"Transform things under the purview of the arcana into other things under the arcana is extremely broad. However, the examples seem to indicate that there are unwritten catagories at work. At some point you're not patterning anymore, you've started making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T01:42:18-07:00","id":928644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928641#post928641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transform things under the purview of the arcana into other things under the arcana is extremely broad. However, the examples seem to indicate that there are unwritten catagories at work. At some point you're not patterning anymore, you've started making.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can arbitrarily speculate and infer all sorts of things from the example spells, but that's not supported by the Practice descriptions themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 07-09-2016, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T05:07:18-07:00","id":928690,"title":"","content":"Ok, so don't bother with Making spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T08:02:19-07:00","id":928736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928590#post928590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making spells in many instances can create things that are Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is how I read Making spells as well, but a few of them threw me off. Create Ghost has Duration as its primary spell factor. Would you say that the Duration talked about is the Duration that the ghost created remains your servant, and then it is a brand new ghost off in the world forever (or until it gets dragged to the Underworld) once the Duration has ended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:42:55-07:00","id":928767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928644#post928644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can arbitrarily speculate and infer all sorts of things from the example spells, but that's not supported by the Practice descriptions themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I agreed with you. My point was that the way around this is to use the spells as examples of the practices working as intended as come to some rough guidelines.<br /> <br /> That is if you actually want to play the game rather than simply whine and pick fights with people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:48:46-07:00","id":928772,"title":"","content":"I operate under assumption that nothing about magic is permanent, with only exceptions being the spells that have Lasting reach options, and cases where the lasting part is a consequence of magic that doesn't require it to continue. This would make all of the Patternings and Unmakings never lasting in my games. <br /> Still, yeah, it's very unclear what is Lasting and what isn't. Currently, you could make a case for all Unmaking spells being duration-bound, which has really interesting implications. Will things be remade when the duration runs out? That's one way to balance it :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:03:45-07:00","id":928784,"title":"","content":"I have no intention to respond to Strill, but on the conversation about Lasting: In my games I have a kind of heuristic: &quot;If it feels like it could be a natural state of being, it can be Lasting. If its something obviously magical, it cannot. You could force something Lasting to be non-Lasting by simply giving the spell a Duration beyond Transitory and spending a Reach, then yes, the Lasting effect reverts at the end of the duration magically.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:12:57-07:00","id":928792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928736#post928736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how I read Making spells as well, but a few of them threw me off. Create Ghost has Duration as its primary spell factor. Would you say that the Duration talked about is the Duration that the ghost created remains your servant, and then it is a brand new ghost off in the world forever (or until it gets dragged to the Underworld) once the Duration has ended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it says that the ghost &quot;remains&quot; instead of the ghost &quot;lasts&quot; I assume that yes, after the Duration of the spell, providing they have no anchors to hold them they go to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> So, looking over the Making spells that are given as examples there seem to be a number of inconsistencies that I assume happen because the arcana were written by different authors. All of Prime's Making spells come with a +2 Reach option to make their effects Lasting, but there aren't any other Making spells in the book that do so even though the Spirit Making spells, Create Ghost, Create Avernian Gate, Psychic Genesis, and Ex Nihilo would logically have those options if Eidolon does. Instead those spells seem to sort of assume that the created beings continue to function as an automatic fact of their existence, especially in the case of Birth Spirit which has Potency as its Primary Factor instead of Duration despite the fact that Potency does nothing for the spell. The only exception to this seems to be the Life Making spell that allows you to whip up original organisms from nothing which specifically says that a creature created with the spell dies when the Duration ends. Create Sympathy explicitly calls its effects out as Lasting and doesn't require Reach to make it so.<br /> <br /> I think I'm personally going to end up houseruling that Making spells don't require +2 Reach and their effects are Lasting, Duration simply determines how long you have direct control of or are able to monitor your creation via spell maintenance (And incidentally dispel it as part of spell maintenance). The exception will be some spells like Temporal Pocket, and Psychic Possession and the like which I'll probably downgrade to Patterning anyways since they're not creating anything just changing the essential nature of things that already exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:27:00-07:00","id":929047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928784#post928784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games I have a kind of heuristic: &quot;If it feels like it could be a natural state of being, it can be Lasting. If its something obviously magical, it cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eidolons are obviously magical, but they can be lasting. Steel that's a hundred times tougher than diamonds is obviously magical, but it can be Lasting with Alter Integrity. Grimoires are obviously magical, but they're lasting. Hallows are magical, but they're lasting. Time paradoxes are obviously magical, but they're lasting. That's about half of the examples of magic labeled in the book as &quot;lasting&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could force something Lasting to be non-Lasting by simply giving the spell a Duration beyond Transitory and spending a Reach, then yes, the Lasting effect reverts at the end of the duration magically.&quot; </div> </div> </div>So you can cast an unmaking spell that un-kills its target when the duration expires?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928767#post928767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, I agreed with you. My point was that the way around this is to use the spells as examples of the practices working as intended as come to some rough guidelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>See that goes completely against the whole point of having Practices in the first place. It was supposed to be one of the main goals of 2nd edition to have internally consistent practices. That way you could feel confident in making creative thaumaturgy spells by the rules, and not according to some nebulous arbitrary sense of &quot;game balance&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is if you actually want to play the game rather than simply whine and pick fights with people. </div> </div> </div>How do you fix flaws without first exposing them? If that's what you call &quot;whining&quot;, then I don't know what I can do to fix that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928690#post928690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so don't bother with Making spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then that introduces even more problems with the 5th arcana dot being exceptionally weak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928792#post928792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, looking over the Making spells that are given as examples there seem to be a number of inconsistencies that I assume happen because the arcana were written by different authors. All of Prime's Making spells come with a +2 Reach option to make their effects Lasting, but there aren't any other Making spells in the book that do so even though the Spirit Making spells, Create Ghost, Create Avernian Gate, Psychic Genesis, and Ex Nihilo would logically have those options if Eidolon does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly suspect that Eidolon can be made lasting because it's an advanced version of Platonic Form, which can also be made lasting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead those spells seem to sort of assume that the created beings continue to function as an automatic fact of their existence, especially in the case of Birth Spirit which has Potency as its Primary Factor instead of Duration despite the fact that Potency does nothing for the spell. The only exception to this seems to be the Life Making spell that allows you to whip up original organisms from nothing which specifically says that a creature created with the spell dies when the Duration ends. Create Sympathy explicitly calls its effects out as Lasting and doesn't require Reach to make it so. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Create Sympathy's effects do wear off over time naturally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I'm personally going to end up houseruling that Making spells don't require +2 Reach and their effects are Lasting, Duration simply determines how long you have direct control of or are able to monitor your creation via spell maintenance (And incidentally dispel it as part of spell maintenance). The exception will be some spells like Temporal Pocket, and Psychic Possession and the like which I'll probably downgrade to Patterning anyways since they're not creating anything just changing the essential nature of things that already exist. </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. My concern is, could a Making spell be dispelled after it has been released? If not, then how do you deal with, for example, a Lasting Ban?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 07-10-2016, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T22:04:33-07:00","id":929059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929047#post929047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you fix flaws except by first exposing them? If that's what you call &quot;whining&quot;, then I don't know what I can do to fix that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've previously demonstrated that you did not know what word economy was back when the wordcount for this book was first shared and that you apply the terms of what Patterning can do absurdly literally (turning a mote of Essence into a sentient creature made of <i>many</i> motes of Essence or a point of Mana into a place that <i>generates</i> Mana is not a sensible reading of &quot;turn one thing in the Arcanum's purview into another thing in the Arcanum's purview&quot; no matter which way you slice it).<br /> <br /> When you are incapable of using basic discernment to figure out obvious things from the provided mechanics, imply that every sideways exploitation of the game language be covered explicitly, and outright <i>make up</i> things to complain about from that confluence of errors, <i>that is whining.</i> What you can do to fix that is <i>exercise even a modicum of common sense</i> instead of playing semantic gotcha-games that will realistically never come up in practical execution.<br /> <br /> The intermediate Practices' effects are slightly more limited than a totally-literal read that disregards conservation would suggest; this is a consequence of brevity and generality in phrasing, not an unforgivable flaw or a sign that being able to add or subtract things from existence without acquiring raw materials to transform is utterly inferior to being able to make water from stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T22:28:07-07:00","id":929064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929059#post929059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've previously demonstrated that you did not know what word economy was back when the wordcount for this book was first shared and that you apply the terms of what Patterning can do absurdly literally (turning a mote of Essence into a sentient creature made of <i>many</i> motes of Essence or a point of Mana into a place that <i>generates</i> Mana is not a sensible reading of &quot;turn one thing in the Arcanum's purview into another thing in the Arcanum's purview&quot; no matter which way you slice it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that absurd? I can turn a human being made of a hundred pounds of meat into a grizzly bear made of 600 pounds of meat with no problem, but I can't exercise the same principle with any other arcanum? I can use Life and Matter to transmogrify a dog into a statue, but I can't turn a statue into a dog?<br /> <br /> If I can turn inanimate things into animate things, and I can turn small things into bigger things, then why can't I turn an inanimate mote of essence into a living spirit? Awakened magic functions on Patterns and Practices, not on conservation of matter or energy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you are incapable of using basic discernment to figure out obvious things from the provided mechanics, </div> </div> </div>The pot calling the kettle black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 07-10-2016, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T23:30:00-07:00","id":929079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929064#post929064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pot calling the kettle black.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a lot to say in regards to this thread now that I'm bothering to look into it, but, uh, this is the funniest and most ill-informed opinion here. Satchel's demonstrably one of the keenest readers and interpreters of these games and their mechanics on the forum to date. He is very capable of using basic discernment to figure out obvious things from the provided mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T23:56:47-07:00","id":929088,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a>: FWIW, at my table, I require Patterning spells to account for differences in the &quot;intensity&quot; of the phenomena involved. This is made explicit for Forces (p146), but I couldn't find any guidance for the other Arcana. As an example, though, I would let a mage with Death 4 transform ghosts into an Avernian Gate, but I would require many ghosts (exact number depending on rank), which requires the requisite scale factor (and potency to overcome rank), of course. Does that address your concerns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T00:51:00-07:00","id":929102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wologimbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929088#post929088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a>: FWIW, at my table, I require Patterning spells to account for differences in the &quot;intensity&quot; of the phenomena involved. This is made explicit for Forces (p146), but I couldn't find any guidance for the other Arcana. As an example, though, I would let a mage with Death 4 transform ghosts into an Avernian Gate, but I would require many ghosts (exact number depending on rank), which requires the requisite scale factor (and potency to overcome rank), of course. Does that address your concerns?</div> </div> </div> </div>Partly. It's a really good idea, but it still doesn't fit with the example spells. There are plenty of example Patterning spells that give you more back than you started with, and there are some Making spells that require reagents in the same way you describe for Patterning spells. In order to make this idea work, you need some way to judge something's metaphysical &quot;weight&quot;, and several arcana defy any attempts at doing this.<br /> <br /> For example, Life transformation spells have no regard for the subject's mass, size, shape, or kingdom, and can create more flesh than they started with, even at only Life 3. Should these spells be Making spells?<br /> <br /> Space patterning spells can enlarge a room's size. Is this not Making by the standards of your principle?<br /> <br /> Create Truth creates Hallows, but it costs 5 mana per potency, plus another 5 mana to make it Lasting. In other words, it works in the way you say Patterning spells should work. Shouldn't it therefore be a Patterning spell, rather than Making?<br /> <br /> Likewise Birth Spirit requires a source of dormant essence to create a Spirit. Should it therefore be a Patterning spell?<br /> <br /> Death 2 can create Ectoplasm out of nothing. How much ectoplasm does it take to make other death-related phenomena?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 07-10-2016, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T06:15:00-07:00","id":929211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929047#post929047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Create Sympathy's effects do wear off over time naturally.<br /> <br /> I like this idea. My concern is, could a Making spell be dispelled after it has been released? If not, then how do you deal with, for example, a Lasting Ban?</div> </div> </div> </div>So what if it fades? That's not the point of what I was saying.<br /> <br /> Obviously an effect created by the arcana can be dismantled by the arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T06:42:53-07:00","id":929217,"title":"","content":"Death 2 doesn't create Ectoplasm (even if it says that it creates it). It commands Ectoplasm out of your body, like a bodily fluid. It's probably a function of Death-inside-you to produce ectoplasm or something. It's like using a Ruling Spell to make Cow produce milk.<br /> It's still rather pointless, because there are literally t5 times when word &quot;Ectoplasm&quot; shows up in the book, two of which are in Ectoplasm related spells, two in listings of Death purview, and one in description of plasms. I still don't understand it's purpose or why is it such a big deal that it deserves it's own purview point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-10-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T06:58:28-07:00","id":929218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See that goes completely against the whole point of having Practices in the first place. It was supposed to be one of the main goals of 2nd edition to have internally consistent practices. That way you could feel confident in making creative thaumaturgy spells by the rules, and not according to some nebulous arbitrary sense of &quot;game balance&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Okay. So? It's written now. I guess it failed in that objective. Move on. You can complain all day and the text won't change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you fix flaws without first exposing them? If that's what you call &quot;whining&quot;, then I don't know what I can do to fix that. </div> </div> </div>My exasperation is from you ignoring attempts to fix it or account for it and just reiterating that there's an inconsistency. That suggests you aren't interested in a solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T07:48:49-07:00","id":929227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929047#post929047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then that introduces even more problems with the 5th arcana dot being exceptionally weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase: do whatever you want, since it's clear you're not interested in any of our advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:17:41-07:00","id":929321,"title":"","content":"Not trying to dogpile here, but to add to that a bit:<br /> <br /> It really feels like most of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> based complaints about the systems stem from a simple issue. Instead of acknowledging that - whatever an individual's personal preferences for game writing styles - the CofD books are written in the natural language style and need to be analyzed from that perspective, a lot of the &quot;problems&quot; identified for &quot;fixing&quot; are really just insisting on reading the text as technical language writing style phrasing.<br /> <br /> Which is really a shame because I really do think you're a good critical reader that could help identify and solve problems in the game text, but it's the refusal to engage with the way the books are written that seems to always dominate these things. Hell, I have a feeling it would be a lot more constructive for everyone if you changed your approach to these things from, &quot;my technical reading of the text <i>must</i> mean that this problem is the result of the rules,&quot; to, &quot;Help me write the rules in a more technical writing fashion so they work better for my group.&quot; The Exalted forum has a number of good threads about the later because the semantics aren't getting in the way of doing something useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:12:13-07:00","id":929356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929217#post929217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death 2 doesn't create Ectoplasm (even if it says that it creates it). It commands Ectoplasm out of your body, like a bodily fluid. It's probably a function of Death-inside-you to produce ectoplasm or something. It's like using a Ruling Spell to make Cow produce milk.<br /> It's still rather pointless, because there are literally t5 times when word &quot;Ectoplasm&quot; shows up in the book, two of which are in Ectoplasm related spells, two in listings of Death purview, and one in description of plasms. I still don't understand it's purpose or why is it such a big deal that it deserves it's own purview point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have my books with me and I never had a PDF of this specific one, but if you look at the write-up of mediums in Second Sight, I think there is some more description of Ectoplasm including (if I remember correctly) a statement saying that it is something that can be called up from any human.<br /> My guess is that they wanted to include it because it is a part of what many people think of when you touch on ghosts in fiction (and &quot;real&quot; mediums).<br /> It's also a thing in Geist.<br /> <br /> To further comment on the description of the Ectoplasm spell, I find that there are several spells that have the same kind of unclear wording. For instance, Forces 2 spells talking about increasing or decreasing a force, when it seems like what you are actually doing, when you look at examples and the practice is focus or diffuse existing forces, not increasing/decreasing them (which should be perfecting or fraying).<br /> In some cases it seems like there are some descriptions that have been brought over from first edition and not changed enough to put the description in line with the practices. <br /> <br /> One of the reasons why I find it hard to discuss things like the current topic right now, is that before the post-errata version of the book comes out, it is hard to say what spells will change descriptions and/or practices, and thus hard to use them as examples to draw understanding from. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/983-mirrorscape","name":"Mirrorscape","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T23:16:44-07:00","id":929581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929218#post929218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really feels like most of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> based complaints about the systems stem from a simple issue. Instead of acknowledging that - whatever an individual's personal preferences for game writing styles - the CofD books are written in the natural language style and need to be analyzed from that perspective, a lot of the &quot;problems&quot; identified for &quot;fixing&quot; are really just insisting on reading the text as technical language writing style phrasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the other Practice description are written well enough to be unambiguous, so I didn't see any reason to treat Patterning any differently. Of course you have questions like &quot;For Weaving spells, what constitutes a 'property'?&quot;, but that's easy enough to infer from the example spells. Patterning, on the other hand, has no limitations at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929218#post929218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My exasperation is from you ignoring attempts to fix it or account for it and just reiterating that there's an inconsistency. That suggests you aren't interested in a solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not ignoring them. I already considered them and couldn't find any consistency with that explanation. So I bring up the same inconsistencies I ran into myself, which lead me to discard that idea.<br /> <br /> For example, you could hypothesize that each Patterning spell is tied to a specific aspect of the arcanum in question, and can only make changes within that aspect. So for example, you could use a Life Patterning spell to change the &quot;species&quot; of a creature, but that spell could not also change the &quot;health&quot; of the creature at the same time.<br /> <br /> Of course, that idea is nonsense because you've got spells like Chaos Mastery that can do everything at once, or Temporal Stutter which can change both a target's time and location, or Shapechange, that can both change species, and transform inert matter into flesh simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T23:43:15-07:00","id":929586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929581#post929581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the other Practice description are written well enough to be unambiguous, so I didn't see any reason to treat Patterning any differently. Of course you have questions like &quot;For Weaving spells, what constitutes a 'property'?&quot;, but that's easy enough to infer from the example spells. Patterning, on the other hand, has no limitations at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>We understand that the Patterning rules are somewhat vague when it comes to the <b>&quot;Law of Equivalent Exchange&quot;</b>.<br /> <br /> Are you looking for solutions? Or just want us to acknowledge it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T00:03:33-07:00","id":929592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929102#post929102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Partly. It's a really good idea, but it still doesn't fit with the example spells. There are plenty of example Patterning spells that give you more back than you started with, and there are some Making spells that require reagents in the same way you describe for Patterning spells. In order to make this idea work, you need some way to judge something's metaphysical &quot;weight&quot;, and several arcana defy any attempts at doing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it's a house rule, it will naturally require that some of the example spells be tweaked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, Life transformation spells have no regard for the subject's mass, size, shape, or kingdom, and can create more flesh than they started with, even at only Life 3. Should these spells be Making spells?<br /> <br /> Space patterning spells can enlarge a room's size. Is this not Making by the standards of your principle? </div> </div> </div>You seem to have misunderstood. My principle addressed Patterning spells, not Making spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Create Truth creates Hallows, but it costs 5 mana per potency, plus another 5 mana to make it Lasting. In other words, it works in the way you say Patterning spells should work. Shouldn't it therefore be a Patterning spell, rather than Making? </div> </div> </div>If you use my house rule, yes. I think 5 mana per potency is a bit on the cheap side, but those decisions are up to the storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise Birth Spirit requires a source of dormant essence to create a Spirit. Should it therefore be a Patterning spell? </div> </div> </div>I can't really say, since I don't know what exactly the authors mean by &quot;dormant essence.&quot; Rules are give for dormant spirits, of course, but I don't know what is meant here. I would probably just ignore that line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Death 2 can create Ectoplasm out of nothing. How much ectoplasm does it take to make other death-related phenomena? </div> </div> </div>WHW addressed &quot;Ectoplasm out of nothing&quot; above. As to the second point, it's up to the storyteller. If you give me a specific example I could tell you how I would rule.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3809-wologimbat","name":"Wologimbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T00:07:30-07:00","id":929593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929581#post929581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that idea is nonsense because you've got spells like Chaos Mastery that can do everything at once, or Temporal Stutter which can change both a target's time and location, or Shapechange, that can both change species, and transform inert matter into flesh simultaneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos Mastery has already been addressed by the writer as potentially trying to do too much. Temporal Stutter achieves the second effect by incorporating a second Arcana (You have to add Space 2, not just the attainment). Shapechange does the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T01:35:48-07:00","id":929618,"title":"","content":"This discussion is kind of going into the wrong way, because strill is simply assuming, that you can make more out of something because there is that one life spell (Shapechanging), which bends the rules. If you use conservation of mass/energy as for Forces is explicitely stated, you can quite clearly see where the advantages of making spells are. If you are irritated by Shapechanging that much simply require it to use conservation of mass too (a 3.5 m tall grizzly bear with 80 kg is kind of funny) or change it to a level 5 Life spell if you want to get bigger or smaller.<br /> <br /> Also, there are a lot of spells which inherently create something out of nothingness, which cannot be done by transforming, because you simply cannot transform nothing into something, no matter which arcana. Space is probably the easiest example:<br /> <br /> Space: Pocket Dimension.<br /> Creating a pocket dimension is creating space out of no space. You cannot transform space out of no space. No space does not exist, so it does not fall under any arcanum. While you can expand, shrink, alter, space that already exists into different space, you cannot extend existing space into the nothingness. So you could expand your living room, wall up half of it and add a secret door, to create some cool secret room, but that room would still be in your living room. A pocket dimension is nowhere and you have absolutely no way to influence nowhere with space short of making spells.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:09:58-07:00","id":940670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=929618#post929618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion is kind of going into the wrong way, because strill is simply assuming, that you can make more out of something because there is that one life spell (Shapechanging), which bends the rules. If you use conservation of mass/energy as for Forces is explicitely stated, you can quite clearly see where the advantages of making spells are. If you are irritated by Shapechanging that much simply require it to use conservation of mass too (a 3.5 m tall grizzly bear with 80 kg is kind of funny) or change it to a level 5 Life spell if you want to get bigger or smaller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal magic should ignore conservation of mass/energy in the targets though. Why? Because by using magic you introduce more energy into the system, namely magic.<br /> Not sure where such conservation is mentioned for Forces, but look at Control Fire and Transform energy spells. Control fire explicitly raises or lowers the size/intensity of the fire, while Transform Energy lets you raise the level of transformed energy for a Mana or lower it for a Reach.<br /> Conservation of anything only applies within a closed system, magic is an extra factor added into that system.<br /> <br /> The more pertinent question would be the extent to which such increases can be done, the requirements and the costs for them.<br /> <br /> Some of Strill's examples seem feasible, at a cost.<br /> <br /> Taking the example of patterning a ghost out of some Mana instead of Making one directly, I'd make that require Mind 4 (or have an automaton ghost) as well as Prime 4 and Death 4 (Mana and ghost being the purviews affected, respectively). Additionally, while the ghost in a Making spell is the effect itself, and is a reasonable thing to exist on its own (thus lasting if memory serves) the ghost made by this proposed spell would revert into ambient mana after the duration expires. Would also require a suitable amount of mana to do it, and maybe a Reach for the Mind part? Not sure on the supernal balancing game there.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, like HardoreHannes mentions, some things just can't be patterned from existing things. Why use Making? For weird abstract creative spells, to be honest. For someone at a level of Mastery lower dot practices will be suitably more versatile, while the Making one expands the options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:45:51-07:00","id":940692,"title":"","content":"You're basically arguing that you can create a ghost eidolon at a lower dot level (Patterning instead of Making) but with more arcana requirements? My knee jerk reaction is that doesn't seem right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T07:36:55-07:00","id":941176,"title":"","content":"Sometimes Making is just faster or simpler from a technical perspective. With enough spells, time, and effort you could create an Earthquake or Nuclear explosions using just Forces 2, but Forces 5 lets you do it as a single dice-pool and just have it work, making it less subject to external interference.<br /> <br /> That's why Making: because &quot;poof, it's there&quot; is easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:11:42-07:00","id":942041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=940692#post940692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're basically arguing that you can create a ghost eidolon at a lower dot level (Patterning instead of Making) but with more arcana requirements? My knee jerk reaction is that doesn't seem right.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my knee jerk reaction too. But I'm arguing it anyway.<br /> Rationalisationally, because of that sideline in the book where it is pointed out that various arcana can accomplish same results at different dot ratings. But mostly because I can see how you could reasonably do it and I have contrarian tendencies.<br /> <br /> Why the reaction that it's not right? Balance of power of some sort, I guess. That Adepts shouldn't be able to do what Masters can. But given a bit of thought, there's really no reason why they shouldn't, in a system with this much creativity.<br /> <br /> Look at everything the Adept would have to do do get that eidolon/ghost: know a specific other Arcanum at likely Adept level, maybe some extra Reach and/or Mana costs, even maybe a neccessary Sacrament of Tass, no matter how easy that is to get. (did not reference that last one in the previous post, but as I said, not sure where it would fall on the balancing game) The actions of a Mage improvising what they have to the effect they want, combinging things and Reaching and complicating the spell. The Master, on the other hand, will just go &quot;Right, sure, I do hereby create this.&quot;<br /> <br /> As seems to be the case in several other things of theirs I've read, Strill does have one part I agree with, then takes it in a direction I'd rather just dismiss offhand. Namely, I do feel some printed spell examples don't neccessarily fall under Making. I have no real explanation to this (gut feeling is that they wanted something balanced and applicable and had no better ideas so shoehorned some things) but I'm not really too bothered with it.<br /> <br /> And while I don't have proper examples in mind at the moment, I believe Making and Unmaking spells could/should be able to achieve some things so abstract that in other systems would ask for a sanity check just to consider such things. (What happens when you Unmake the Time - as in, the abstract notion of being connected to time, rather than one segment of it - of a person? Could you create a Tass-analogue of other Arcana's abstracter purviews? What would be the consequences of Making new goetia for yourself, long-term?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","user":"Aeryes","date":".  clarification 08-02-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:48:44-07:00","id":943619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=928590#post928590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making spells in many instances can create things that are Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would this be different for Patterning? If the thing you Pattern'd can exist in its new state, why would it change again once the duration is up? That would require more energy than just staying in its new, sustainable form. Would be a bit odd if teleportation spells pulled you back when the duration ends, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:20:33-07:00","id":943813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=943619#post943619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would this be different for Patterning? If the thing you Pattern'd can exist in its new state, why would it change again once the duration is up? That would require more energy than just staying in its new, sustainable form. Would be a bit odd if teleportation spells pulled you back when the duration ends, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being in a new location is a side effect of the spell, the actual spell is that you rewrite your location, where doesn't really matter for the purpose of what the spell does. Hence why where you end up is Lasting. Making spells, at least pre-errata had options which were the same as the effects of the spell but were Lasting in spite of that. For instance, there wasn't anything natural about Eidolon, but it could be made to be Lasting. Now that they've removed that kind of thing generally Making falls more in line with the way lesser Practices do in terms of Lasting and Duration, etc, though there is still, imo, some confusion about say Birth Spirit or Create Ghost. That could just as easily be chalked up to me reading what I want to read into those spells though.<br /> <br /> TL;DR Yes, Patterning can have side effects that are Lasting, as can any of the Practices, but Making spells had the distinction of creating Lasting effects that weren't side effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:19:06-07:00","id":944392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928581-why-care-about-making-spells-when-you-have-patterning?p=943813#post943813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being in a new location is a side effect of the spell, the actual spell is that you rewrite your location, where doesn't really matter for the purpose of what the spell does. Hence why where you end up is Lasting. Making spells, at least pre-errata had options which were the same as the effects of the spell but were Lasting in spite of that. For instance, there wasn't anything natural about Eidolon, but it could be made to be Lasting. Now that they've removed that kind of thing generally Making falls more in line with the way lesser Practices do in terms of Lasting and Duration, etc, though there is still, imo, some confusion about say Birth Spirit or Create Ghost. That could just as easily be chalked up to me reading what I want to read into those spells though.<br /> <br /> TL;DR Yes, Patterning can have side effects that are Lasting, as can any of the Practices, but Making spells had the distinction of creating Lasting effects that weren't side effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing anywhere in the rules that suggests only &quot;side effects&quot; of spells can be automatically Lasting (without needing to be called out in the description), and your argument with teleportation seems very nebulous. Even if you could argue that &quot;where&quot; does not matter for the spell (and I doubt it, your current location and your target location are very likely part of the very fabric of the spell), &quot;not being where I am right now&quot; and &quot;being where I want to be&quot; are the direct focus of the spell, not a side effect. The book specifically quotes healing to be Lasting as an example, and surely removing wounds is the direct purpose of the spell, not a side effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:59:01-07:00","id":944444,"title":"","content":"It's generally inconsistent and given the choice, you are probably better off assuming that all spells that don't mention being Lasting are not Lasting, while applying some common sense (I dislike saying this, believe me) to spells that have side effects that remain lasting, like teleportation. <br /> It's one of areas where game could be improved massively if it had some better formatting / spell writing, even a line of text &quot;Lasting: Yes/No/Partially&quot;. Like, I would never even start thinking about how any part of Crucible might be Lasting; this lack of clarity might cause a lot of miscommunications between Storytellers and players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:01:30-07:00","id":944445,"title":"","content":"The spell is: Heal x amount of damage. The side effect is indeed the healed flesh and since that's the natural state of the flesh it's Lasting. Not -only- side effects of spells are Lasting, but it's usually that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:08:35-07:00","id":944451,"title":"","content":"Why is something being natural state important to this? I'm seriously confused, I'm kinda weak lately due to sleep deprivation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:03:52-07:00","id":944478,"title":"","content":"In some cases it's not but it seems to generally be the case that Lasting works because its effects can be sustained without further magic. That's how I understand it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:35:15-07:00","id":944565,"title":"","content":"We are sort of spreading the same conversation (the one on Lasting) over two threads, and as Lasting isn't directly under the original topic here, I recommend we continue here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page77\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...edition/page77</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}